// Regression: a read from an OPEN map (empty {} literal, value type not yet
// fixed) used to default the read to string, and a read-modify-write store
// (m[k] = m[k] + 1) then FIXED the map's value type to string - so the other
// branch's `m[k] = 1` was rejected ("Cannot store int in map with values of
// string"). The book's word-count pattern. The RMW's non-map operand now
// drives the inference: the map becomes an int map end-to-end.
// EXPECT: 2
fn main() {
    counts = {}
    word = "apple"
    if (counts.has(word)) {
        counts[word] = counts[word] + 1
    } else {
        counts[word] = 1
    }
    counts[word] = counts[word] + 1
    print("${counts[word]}")
}
